<section class="view" id="view-disclaimer">
<div class="card panel disclaimer-panel">
<h3>Educational use</h3>
<p>The Fellowship Examination SCQ App (FEx SCQ) is an educational resource created and developed by
Dr Daryl Goh for ACEM trainees preparing for the Fellowship Written SCQ Examination. It is provided
free of charge for personal study and revision.</p>
<p>Nothing in this app constitutes clinical advice or a directive for patient care. Clinical
decisions must always be made with reference to current guidelines, local protocols and appropriate
senior supervision.</p>
</div>

<div class="card panel disclaimer-panel">
<h3>No affiliation with ACEM</h3>
<p>This app is not officially endorsed by, affiliated with, or approved by the Australasian College
for Emergency Medicine (ACEM). It is not an official ACEM examination product, and it is not
produced, reviewed or sanctioned by the College.</p>
<p>Question content is written independently. Any resemblance to material used in an actual ACEM
examination is coincidental, and no question here is drawn from a live or past College examination
paper.</p>
</div>

<div class="card panel disclaimer-panel">
<h3>Accuracy of content</h3>
<p><strong>Not every question in this app has been individually verified as correct.</strong> The
question bank is large and has been assembled with the assistance of automated tools. Errors in
answers, explanations and learning points are possible.</p>
<p>You should treat every item as a prompt for further reading rather than as a definitive source.
Always apply your own clinical judgement and confirm anything you intend to rely on against current
primary sources, college curricula and established textbooks. If you find an error, verify it
against a trusted reference before committing it to memory.</p>
</div>

<div class="card panel disclaimer-panel">
<h3>Your data</h3>
<p>Progress, bookmarks and settings are stored only in this browser on this device. Nothing is
uploaded, and no account is required. Clearing your browser storage will erase your recorded
progress.</p>
</div>
