ate with metabolic acidosis. A major error is stopping insulin when glucose normalises before ketonaemia clears.","learningPoint":"Diabetic ketoacidosis: elevated beta-hydroxybutyrate with metabolic acidosis. Avoid stopping insulin when glucose normalises before ketonaemia clears.","id":"endocrine-002","globalNumber":202},{"category":"Endocrine","categoryNumber":3,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"In a patient being assessed for diabetic ketoacidosis, which finding is the most discriminating and should carry the greatest diagnostic weight?","options":["marked effective osmolality with little acidosis","significant ketonaemia with glucose below the usual DKA range","elevated beta-hydroxybutyrate with metabolic acidosis","severe multisystem decompensation rather than thyroid hormone level alone","hypotension refractory to fluid in a steroid-dependent or adrenal patient"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"elevated beta-hydroxybutyrate with metabolic acidosis","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is elevated beta-hydroxybutyrate with metabolic acidosis. In context, this supports Diabetic ketoacidosis and should trigger: give isotonic fluid, commence fixed-rate insulin after checking potassium and replace electrolytes.","learningPoint":"Diabetic ketoacidosis: elevated beta-hydroxybutyrate with metabolic acidosis. Avoid stopping insulin when glucose normalises before ketonaemia clears.","id":"endocrine-003","globalNumber":203},{"category":"Endocrine","categoryNumber":4,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"During emergency management of diabetic ketoacidosis, which action is specifically hazardous or most likely to delay definitive care?","options":["delaying steroids until cortisol results return","administering iodine before blocking new hormone synthesis","rapidly lowering osmolality or giving early high-dose insulin before fluids","stopping insulin when glucose normalises before ketonaemia clears","dismissing ketoacidosis because the glucose is