ing new hormone synthesis"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"dismissing ketoacidosis because the glucose is not markedly elevated","explanation":"The hazardous action is dismissing ketoacidosis because the glucose is not markedly elevated. It can worsen physiology, delay definitive treatment and contribute to refractory acidosis and hypokalaemia.","learningPoint":"Euglycaemic ketoacidosis from an SGLT2 inhibitor: significant ketonaemia with glucose below the usual DKA range. Avoid dismissing ketoacidosis because the glucose is not markedly elevated.","id":"endocrine-014","globalNumber":214},{"category":"Endocrine","categoryNumber":15,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient with euglycaemic ketoacidosis from an sglt2 inhibitor initially stabilises. Which serious complication should be specifically anticipated and monitored for?","options":["arrhythmia, high-output failure and hepatic dysfunction","cerebral oedema, seizures and vascular thrombosis","cerebral oedema, hypokalaemia and treatment-related hypoglycaemia","refractory shock and life-threatening hyperkalaemia","refractory acidosis and hypokalaemia"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"refractory acidosis and hypokalaemia","explanation":"The important complication is refractory acidosis and hypokalaemia. Ongoing reassessment is required even after initial stabilisation of euglycaemic ketoacidosis from an sglt2 inhibitor.","learningPoint":"Euglycaemic ketoacidosis from an SGLT2 inhibitor: significant ketonaemia with glucose below the usual DKA range. Avoid dismissing ketoacidosis because the glucose is not markedly elevated.","id":"endocrine-015","globalNumber":215},{"category":"Endocrine","categoryNumber":16,"type":"diagnosis","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient presents with fever, agitation, tachyarrhythmia, heart failure and gastrointestinal dysfunction in thyrotoxicosis. Which diagnosis best accounts for the complete pattern?","options":["Thyroid storm","Phaeochromocytoma crisis","Adrenal crisis","Seroto