st diagnostic weight?","options":["inappropriately low urine osmolality despite hypernatraemia","pericarditis in severe azotaemia without the typical diffuse ECG pattern","progressive ECG toxicity in the setting of elevated potassium","neurologic deterioration temporally related to rapid urea removal","polyuria exceeding expected physiologic clearance after decompression"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"progressive ECG toxicity in the setting of elevated potassium","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is progressive ECG toxicity in the setting of elevated potassium. In context, this supports Life-threatening hyperkalaemia and should trigger: give intravenous calcium immediately, shift potassium intracellularly and arrange definitive removal.","learningPoint":"Life-threatening hyperkalaemia: progressive ECG toxicity in the setting of elevated potassium. Avoid delaying membrane stabilisation while awaiting a repeat laboratory sample.","id":"renal-003","globalNumber":253},{"category":"Renal","categoryNumber":4,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"During emergency management of life-threatening hyperkalaemia, which action is specifically hazardous or most likely to delay definitive care?","options":["using potassium-containing fluid or delaying treatment until oliguria is established","continuing high-efficiency dialysis despite evolving neurology","rapidly correcting chronic hypernatraemia","delaying membrane stabilisation while awaiting a repeat laboratory sample","routine bicarbonate or mannitol use without an individual indication"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"delaying membrane stabilisation while awaiting a repeat laboratory sample","explanation":"The hazardous action is delaying membrane stabilisation while awaiting a repeat laboratory sample. It can worsen physiology, delay definitive treatment and contribute to ventricular fibrillation or asystole.","learningPoint":"Life-threatening hyperkalaemia: progressive ECG toxicity in the setting of elevated pot