, which action is specifically hazardous or most likely to delay definitive care?","options":["estimating injury severity from skin burns alone","assuming deterioration will stop immediately after tick removal","transporting before effective cooling when safe on-site immersion is available","assuming fixed dilated pupils indicate irreversible death","routine prophylactic antibiotics or diuretics without indication"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"assuming fixed dilated pupils indicate irreversible death","explanation":"The hazardous action is assuming fixed dilated pupils indicate irreversible death. It can worsen physiology, delay definitive treatment and contribute to arrhythmia, delayed neurologic injury and rhabdomyolysis.","learningPoint":"Lightning injury: keraunoparalysis or Lichtenberg figures with a compatible event. Avoid assuming fixed dilated pupils indicate irreversible death.","id":"environmental-emergency-medicine-049","globalNumber":679},{"category":"Environmental","categoryNumber":50,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient with lightning injury initially stabilises. Which serious complication should be specifically anticipated and monitored for?","options":["ventricular fibrillation, coagulopathy and afterdrop","arrhythmia, compartment syndrome and renal failure","respiratory arrest and aspiration","fulminant hepatic failure, DIC and rhabdomyolysis","arrhythmia, delayed neurologic injury and rhabdomyolysis"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"arrhythmia, delayed neurologic injury and rhabdomyolysis","explanation":"The important complication is arrhythmia, delayed neurologic injury and rhabdomyolysis. Ongoing reassessment is required even after initial stabilisation of lightning injury.","learningPoint":"Lightning injury: keraunoparalysis or Lichtenberg figures with a compatible event. Avoid assuming fixed dilated pupils indicate irreversible death.","id":"environmental-emergency-medicine-050","globalNumber":680},{"category":"Medical Administrat