ryNumber":20,"type":"calculation","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A diagnostic study reports TP=81, FN=19, FP=9, and TN=191. What is the positive likelihood ratio?","options":["0.20","0.81","0.91","0.90","18.00"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"18.00","explanation":"Sensitivity=0.810; specificity=0.955. Positive Likelihood Ratio = sensitivity / (1 - specificity) = 18.00.","learningPoint":"Use the correct denominator for positive likelihood ratio.","id":"medical-administration-and-statistics-020","globalNumber":700},{"category":"Medical Administration","categoryNumber":21,"type":"calculation","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"In a randomised trial, the adverse outcome occurred in 28% of controls and 18% of treated patients. What is the number needed to treat, rounded up?","options":["10","4","2","6","3"],"answerIndex":0,"answer":"10","explanation":"Absolute risk reduction = 0.28 - 0.18 = 0.10. NNT = 1/ARR = 10.00, rounded up to 10.","learningPoint":"NNT uses absolute, not relative, risk reduction and is always rounded up.","id":"medical-administration-and-statistics-021","globalNumber":701},{"category":"Medical Administration","categoryNumber":22,"type":"calculation","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"In a randomised trial, the adverse outcome occurred in 12% of controls and 8% of treated patients. What is the number needed to treat, rounded up?","options":["3","26","4","8","12"],"answerIndex":1,"answer":"26","explanation":"Absolute risk reduction = 0.12 - 0.08 = 0.04. NNT = 1/ARR = 25.00, rounded up to 26.","learningPoint":"NNT uses absolute, not relative, risk reduction and is always rounded up.","id":"medical-administration-and-statistics-022","globalNumber":702},{"category":"Medical Administration","categoryNumber":23,"type":"calculation","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"In a randomised trial, the adverse outcome occurred in 42% of controls and 30% of treated patients. What is the number needed to treat, rounded up?","options":["12","2","9","3","4"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"9","explanation":"A