l death","maternal and fetal death from prolonged low-flow state"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"maternal and fetal death from prolonged low-flow state","explanation":"The important complication is maternal and fetal death from prolonged low-flow state. Ongoing reassessment is required even after initial stabilisation of resuscitative hysterotomy.","learningPoint":"Resuscitative hysterotomy: maternal circulation improves when aortocaval compression is relieved. Avoid delaying for fetal assessment, consent formalities or theatre transfer.","id":"obstetrics-and-gynaecology-100","globalNumber":1350},{"category":"Cardiovascular","categoryNumber":101,"type":"diagnosis","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient presents with ongoing ischaemic chest pain with upsloping ST depression and tall symmetrical precordial T waves without classic anterior ST elevation. Which diagnosis best explains the overall clinical pattern?","options":["De Winter anterior occlusion myocardial infarction","Right ventricular myocardial infarction","Wellens syndrome","Kounis syndrome","Spontaneous coronary artery dissection"],"answerIndex":0,"answer":"De Winter anterior occlusion myocardial infarction","explanation":"The presentation is most consistent with De Winter anterior occlusion myocardial infarction. The key discriminator is the De Winter pattern indicating acute proximal LAD occlusion. Immediate priorities include: activate the primary PCI pathway as an occlusion myocardial infarction without waiting for ST elevation.","learningPoint":"De Winter anterior occlusion myocardial infarction: the De Winter pattern indicating acute proximal LAD occlusion. Avoid treating the tracing as low-risk non-ST-elevation ACS and delaying reperfusion.","id":"cardiovascular-101","globalNumber":1351,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Cardiovascular","categoryNumber":102,"type":"management","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient has de winter anterior occlusion myocardial infarction: ongoing ischaemic chest pai