t no clear thrombus?","options":["obtain urgent echocardiography and cardiothoracic advice for anticoagulation, thrombolysis or surgery","obtain urgent multimodal valve imaging and cardiothoracic surgical review","obtain blood cultures, start appropriate intravenous antibiotics and seek urgent surgical review","support perfusion with afterload reduction when feasible and arrange emergency surgery","stabilise with afterload reduction and mechanical support while arranging emergency surgery"],"answerIndex":1,"answer":"obtain urgent multimodal valve imaging and cardiothoracic surgical review","explanation":"The priority is to obtain urgent multimodal valve imaging and cardiothoracic surgical review. The decisive feature is fixed prosthetic obstruction with dense subvalvular tissue rather than mobile thrombus. A major error is assuming every obstructed prosthetic valve should receive thrombolysis.","learningPoint":"Mechanical prosthetic valve dysfunction from pannus: fixed prosthetic obstruction with dense subvalvular tissue rather than mobile thrombus. Avoid assuming every obstructed prosthetic valve should receive thrombolysis.","id":"cardiovascular-197","globalNumber":1447,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Cardiovascular","categoryNumber":198,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which investigation or clinical feature is most specific for mechanical prosthetic valve dysfunction from pannus in this presentation?","options":["restricted leaflet motion with an abrupt rise in transvalvular gradient","severe eccentric acute mitral regurgitation on echocardiography","fixed prosthetic obstruction with dense subvalvular tissue rather than mobile thrombus","premature mitral valve closure and severe regurgitation with a non-dilated left ventricle","severely restricted aortic valve opening with a high gradient or low-flow severe stenosis"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"fixed prosthetic obstruction with dense subvalvular tissue rather than mobile thrombus","e