ror is labeling the illness as routine community-acquired pneumonia despite rapid non-response.","learningPoint":"Acute interstitial pneumonia: diffuse alveolar damage after exclusion of infection, cardiac failure and known causes. Avoid labeling the illness as routine community-acquired pneumonia despite rapid non-response.","id":"respiratory-157","globalNumber":1507,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Respiratory","categoryNumber":158,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which investigation or clinical feature is most specific for acute interstitial pneumonia in this presentation?","options":["rapid onset after forceful inspiration against an obstructed airway","lipoproteinaceous alveolar material with impaired gas exchange and no hydrostatic cause","diffuse alveolar damage after exclusion of infection, cardiac failure and known causes","pulmonary oedema confined predominantly to the recently re-expanded lung","progressively bloodier bronchoalveolar lavage aliquots"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"diffuse alveolar damage after exclusion of infection, cardiac failure and known causes","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is diffuse alveolar damage after exclusion of infection, cardiac failure and known causes. In context, this supports Acute interstitial pneumonia and should prompt clinicians to provide lung-protective critical care and early specialist diagnostic evaluation.","learningPoint":"Acute interstitial pneumonia: diffuse alveolar damage after exclusion of infection, cardiac failure and known causes. Avoid labeling the illness as routine community-acquired pneumonia despite rapid non-response.","id":"respiratory-158","globalNumber":1508,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Respiratory","categoryNumber":159,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which action could directly worsen physiology or delay definitive treatment in acute interstitial pneumonia?","options":["excluding the diagnosis because the peripheral eosino