and expiratory flow or direct imaging of tracheal obstruction"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"failure to pass suction catheter with air tracking into neck tissues","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is failure to pass suction catheter with air tracking into neck tissues. In context, this supports Tracheostomy displacement with false passage and should prompt clinicians to remove the displaced tube, oxygenate from above if possible and re-establish the airway with expert help.","learningPoint":"Tracheostomy displacement with false passage: failure to pass suction catheter with air tracking into neck tissues. Avoid blindly forcing a tube through an immature tracheostomy tract.","id":"respiratory-183","globalNumber":1533,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Respiratory","categoryNumber":184,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"During emergency management of tracheostomy displacement with false passage, which action is most hazardous or most likely to delay definitive care?","options":["repeatedly ventilating through a blocked tube without checking patency","delaying intubation until laryngoscopy becomes impossible","misdiagnosing fixed stridor as refractory asthma","blindly forcing a tube through an immature tracheostomy tract","inserting repeated chest tubes without investigating airway disruption"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"blindly forcing a tube through an immature tracheostomy tract","explanation":"The hazardous action is blindly forcing a tube through an immature tracheostomy tract. It can worsen physiology or delay definitive care; an important consequence is massive surgical emphysema, pneumomediastinum and hypoxic arrest.","learningPoint":"Tracheostomy displacement with false passage: failure to pass suction catheter with air tracking into neck tissues. Avoid blindly forcing a tube through an immature tracheostomy tract.","id":"respiratory-184","globalNumber":1534,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Respiratory","categoryNumber":