 error is diagnosing septic arthritis from one painful joint without considering migratory pattern and carditis.","learningPoint":"Acute rheumatic fever with carditis: Jones-criteria illness with objective carditis or characteristic valvulitis. Avoid diagnosing septic arthritis from one painful joint without considering migratory pattern and carditis.","id":"paediatrics-187","globalNumber":1917,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Paediatrics","categoryNumber":188,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which feature should carry the greatest diagnostic weight when assessing for acute rheumatic fever with carditis?","options":["at least five days of fever with characteristic mucocutaneous signs and cardiac dysfunction","rapid improvement in perfusion or oxygenation after ductal reopening","Jones-criteria illness with objective carditis or characteristic valvulitis","ventricular dysfunction and myocardial injury disproportionate to respiratory findings","multisystem inflammation with myocardial dysfunction and no better microbial cause"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"Jones-criteria illness with objective carditis or characteristic valvulitis","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is Jones-criteria illness with objective carditis or characteristic valvulitis. In context, this supports Acute rheumatic fever with carditis and should prompt clinicians to treat streptococcal infection, manage heart failure and arrange long-term secondary prophylaxis.","learningPoint":"Acute rheumatic fever with carditis: Jones-criteria illness with objective carditis or characteristic valvulitis. Avoid diagnosing septic arthritis from one painful joint without considering migratory pattern and carditis.","id":"paediatrics-188","globalNumber":1918,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Paediatrics","categoryNumber":189,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which management error should be specifically avoided in acute rheumatic fever with carditis?","opti