 to avoid blind urethral catheterisation and obtain urologic drainage and repair planning. The decisive feature is contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation. A major error is forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma.","learningPoint":"Posterior urethral injury: contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation. Avoid forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma.","id":"trauma-157","globalNumber":2177,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Trauma","categoryNumber":158,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which investigation or clinical feature is most specific for posterior urethral injury in this presentation?","options":["haemodynamic instability with splenic disruption and haemoperitoneum","contrast outlining bowel loops on CT cystography from a bladder-dome rupture","contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation","retroperitoneal gas or contrast leak after a handlebar or seatbelt mechanism","abrupt renal arterial cutoff or absent renal enhancement after trauma"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation. In context, this supports Posterior urethral injury and should prompt clinicians to avoid blind urethral catheterisation and obtain urologic drainage and repair planning.","learningPoint":"Posterior urethral injury: contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation. Avoid forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma.","id":"trauma-158","globalNumber":2178,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Trauma","categoryNumber":159,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which action could directly worsen physiology or delay definitive treatment in posterior urethral injury?","options":["reassuring from minimal haematuria despite a high-risk mechanism","sending an unstable patient for prolonged CT imaging","performing routine contrast CT without dedicated cystography and missing the rupture","forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma","discharging after an initially benign abdominal examination"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma","explanation":"The hazardous action is forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma. It can worsen physiology or delay definitive care; an important consequence is false passage, infection and long-term stricture.","learningPoint":"Posterior urethral injury: contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation. Avoid forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma.","id":"trauma-159","globalNumber":2179,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Trauma","categoryNumber":160,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"After apparent early improvement in posterior urethral injury, which complication remains a major concern?","options":["retroperitoneal haemorrhage, renal loss and hypertension","delayed perforation, pancreatitis and sepsis","uncontrolled retroperitoneal haemorrhage and coagulopathy","exsanguination and coagulopathy","false passage, infection and long-term stricture"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"false passage, infection and long-term stricture","explanation":"The complication to anticipate is false passage, infection and long-term stricture. Continued reassessment is required even after initial stabilisation of posterior urethral injury.","learningPoint":"Posterior urethral injury: contrast extravasation on retrograde urethrography before catheterisation. Avoid forcing a urethral catheter through resistance after pelvic trauma.","id":"trauma-160","globalNumber":2180,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Trauma","categoryNumber":161,"type":"diagnosis","diffi