emorrhage with haemodynamic features not explained by bleeding alone. A major error is waiting for endocrine testing before treating suspected adrenal failure.","learningPoint":"Traumatic adrenal haemorrhage with adrenal crisis: bilateral adrenal haemorrhage with haemodynamic features not explained by bleeding alone. Avoid waiting for endocrine testing before treating suspected adrenal failure.","id":"trauma-172","globalNumber":2192,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Trauma","categoryNumber":173,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient may have traumatic adrenal haemorrhage with adrenal crisis. Which finding most strongly supports this diagnosis over its mimics?","options":["systemic toxicity after reperfusion of crushed muscle","haemodynamic instability with an open-book or vertical-shear pelvic pattern","bilateral adrenal haemorrhage with haemodynamic features not explained by bleeding alone","more than 1500 mL immediate drainage or ongoing major output","pericardial fluid with right-sided collapse in a compatible mechanism"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"bilateral adrenal haemorrhage with haemodynamic features not explained by bleeding alone","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is bilateral adrenal haemorrhage with haemodynamic features not explained by bleeding alone. In context, this supports Traumatic adrenal haemorrhage with adrenal crisis and should prompt clinicians to give stress-dose corticosteroid while continuing trauma resuscitation.","learningPoint":"Traumatic adrenal haemorrhage with adrenal crisis: bilateral adrenal haemorrhage with haemodynamic features not explained by bleeding alone. Avoid waiting for endocrine testing before treating suspected adrenal failure.","id":"trauma-173","globalNumber":2193,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Trauma","categoryNumber":174,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient with traumatic adrenal haemorrhage with adrenal crisis is deteriorating. Which proposed