Point":"Meckel diverticulitis with perforation: an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue. Avoid ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis.","id":"general-surgery-162","globalNumber":2282,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"General surgery","categoryNumber":163,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"In suspected meckel diverticulitis with perforation, which finding is the most discriminating?","options":["free perforation from diseased sigmoid colon with diffuse contamination","sonographic Murphy sign with wall thickening or pericholecystic fluid","an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue","appendiceal collection with contained perforation","pneumoperitoneum with acute generalised peritonitis"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue. In context, this supports Meckel diverticulitis with perforation and should prompt clinicians to give antibiotics and arrange surgical resection.","learningPoint":"Meckel diverticulitis with perforation: an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue. Avoid ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis.","id":"general-surgery-163","globalNumber":2283,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"General surgery","categoryNumber":164,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"During emergency management of meckel diverticulitis with perforation, which action is most hazardous or most likely to delay definitive care?","options":["treating like sigmoid volvulus with colonoscopic decompression","immediate unplanned dissection through a mature inflammatory mass in a stable patient","assuming all gastric pneumatosis is benign emphysema","ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis","assuming a normal common bile duct excludes gallbladder infection"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis","explanation":"The hazardous action is ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis. It can worsen physiology or delay definitive care; an important consequence is perforation, abscess and bowel obstruction.","learningPoint":"Meckel diverticulitis with perforation: an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue. Avoid ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis.","id":"general-surgery-164","globalNumber":2284,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"General surgery","categoryNumber":165,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient with meckel diverticulitis with perforation initially stabilises. Which serious complication should be specifically anticipated?","options":["perforation, groin abscess and sepsis","septic shock and multiorgan failure","recurrent sepsis, fistula and free perforation","gastric necrosis, perforation and septic shock","perforation, abscess and bowel obstruction"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"perforation, abscess and bowel obstruction","explanation":"The complication to anticipate is perforation, abscess and bowel obstruction. Continued reassessment is required even after initial stabilisation of meckel diverticulitis with perforation.","learningPoint":"Meckel diverticulitis with perforation: an inflamed blind-ending ileal diverticulum, sometimes with ectopic tissue. Avoid ending exploration after finding a normal appendix despite ongoing peritonitis.","id":"general-surgery-165","globalNumber":2285,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"General surgery","categoryNumber":166,"type":"diagnosis","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which diagnosis is most likely in a patient with gastric outlet obstruction in an older patient wi