h canal compromise","explanation":"The presentation is most consistent with Thoracolumbar burst fracture with canal compromise. The key discriminator is posterior vertebral-body wall disruption with canal compromise. Immediate priorities include: immobilise, perform complete neurological assessment and obtain urgent spinal surgical review.","learningPoint":"Thoracolumbar burst fracture with canal compromise: posterior vertebral-body wall disruption with canal compromise. Avoid allowing mobilisation based solely on preserved initial motor power.","id":"orthopaedic-121","globalNumber":2391,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Orthopaedic","categoryNumber":122,"type":"management","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A patient has thoracolumbar burst fracture with canal compromise: axial-load trauma causes a comminuted vertebral-body fracture with retropulsed fragments. What is the most appropriate immediate emergency-department management?","options":["maintain immobilisation and obtain urgent spinal assessment, avoiding uncontrolled extension","immobilise, perform complete neurological assessment and obtain urgent spinal surgical review","maintain spinal precautions and actively evaluate for intra-abdominal injury with specialist fixation planning","immobilise and obtain urgent spinal assessment for operative or external stabilisation","maintain rigid immobilisation and obtain urgent CT, MRI and spinal specialist assessment"],"answerIndex":1,"answer":"immobilise, perform complete neurological assessment and obtain urgent spinal surgical review","explanation":"The priority is to immobilise, perform complete neurological assessment and obtain urgent spinal surgical review. The decisive feature is posterior vertebral-body wall disruption with canal compromise. A major error is allowing mobilisation based solely on preserved initial motor power.","learningPoint":"Thoracolumbar burst fracture with canal compromise: posterior vertebral-body wall disruption with canal compromi