ng","explanation":"The priority is to perform urgent gentle reduction and obtain orthopaedic fixation planning. The decisive feature is talar displacement compromising soft tissue and blood supply. A major error is delaying reduction for CT while skin and vascular supply remain threatened.","learningPoint":"Talar neck fracture with threatened skin: talar displacement compromising soft tissue and blood supply. Avoid delaying reduction for CT while skin and vascular supply remain threatened.","id":"orthopaedic-147","globalNumber":2417,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Orthopaedic","categoryNumber":148,"type":"discriminator","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which feature should carry the greatest diagnostic weight when assessing for talar neck fracture with threatened skin?","options":["disruption of talar blood supply with a displaced neck fracture","widening between first and second metatarsal bases or a fleck sign","talar displacement compromising soft tissue and blood supply","proximal fibular fracture with distal tibiofibular syndesmosis disruption","reduced Bohler angle or intra-articular comminution"],"answerIndex":2,"answer":"talar displacement compromising soft tissue and blood supply","explanation":"The most discriminating finding is talar displacement compromising soft tissue and blood supply. In context, this supports Talar neck fracture with threatened skin and should prompt clinicians to perform urgent gentle reduction and obtain orthopaedic fixation planning.","learningPoint":"Talar neck fracture with threatened skin: talar displacement compromising soft tissue and blood supply. Avoid delaying reduction for CT while skin and vascular supply remain threatened.","id":"orthopaedic-148","globalNumber":2418,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Orthopaedic","categoryNumber":149,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which management error should be specifically avoided in talar neck fracture with threatened skin?","options":["delaying reducti