ical repair.","learningPoint":"Acute laryngeal fracture: laryngeal framework disruption with airway compromise. Avoid repeated blind intubation through a disrupted larynx.","id":"head-and-neck-168","globalNumber":2538,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Head and Neck","categoryNumber":169,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which management error should be specifically avoided in acute laryngeal fracture?","options":["packing the ear canal tightly or testing clear fluid with bedside glucose alone","allowing a supine obtunded patient with an unstable tongue-bearing segment","nasotracheal intubation with possible skull-base fracture","repeated blind intubation through a disrupted larynx","aspirating without compression or leaving the collection untreated"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"repeated blind intubation through a disrupted larynx","explanation":"The hazardous action is repeated blind intubation through a disrupted larynx. It can worsen physiology or delay definitive care; an important consequence is complete airway obstruction and long-term voice impairment.","learningPoint":"Acute laryngeal fracture: laryngeal framework disruption with airway compromise. Avoid repeated blind intubation through a disrupted larynx.","id":"head-and-neck-169","globalNumber":2539,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Head and Neck","categoryNumber":170,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Following initial treatment of acute laryngeal fracture, which complication requires focused monitoring?","options":["airway obstruction and deep infection","airway obstruction, massive bleeding and CSF leak","meningitis, facial paralysis and hearing loss","septal abscess, cartilage necrosis and saddle-nose deformity","complete airway obstruction and long-term voice impairment"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"complete airway obstruction and long-term voice impairment","explanation":"The complication to anticipate is complete airway obstruction and long-term voice impair