eatening abnormal uterine bleeding and should prompt clinicians to resuscitate and use rapid hormonal, antifibrinolytic, tamponade or procedural haemostasis as appropriate.","learningPoint":"Life-threatening abnormal uterine bleeding: active uterine bleeding after pregnancy-related causes and coagulopathy are assessed. Avoid delaying haemostatic treatment while waiting for complete outpatient investigation.","id":"obstetrics-and-gynaecology-168","globalNumber":2638,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology","categoryNumber":169,"type":"pitfall","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Which management error should be specifically avoided in life-threatening abnormal uterine bleeding?","options":["inducing labour or failing to arrange serial hCG surveillance","blind curettage without blood-product readiness or consideration of enhanced myometrial vascularity","assuming all cyst rupture is self-limiting despite ongoing shock","delaying haemostatic treatment while waiting for complete outpatient investigation","reassuring from minimal visible vaginal blood despite worsening shock"],"answerIndex":3,"answer":"delaying haemostatic treatment while waiting for complete outpatient investigation","explanation":"The hazardous action is delaying haemostatic treatment while waiting for complete outpatient investigation. It can worsen physiology or delay definitive care; an important consequence is haemorrhagic shock and severe anaemia.","learningPoint":"Life-threatening abnormal uterine bleeding: active uterine bleeding after pregnancy-related causes and coagulopathy are assessed. Avoid delaying haemostatic treatment while waiting for complete outpatient investigation.","id":"obstetrics-and-gynaecology-169","globalNumber":2639,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology","categoryNumber":170,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"Following initial treatment of life-threatening abnormal uterine bleeding, which complication req