y dissection.","id":"obstetrics-and-gynaecology-199","globalNumber":2669,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology","categoryNumber":200,"type":"complication","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"After apparent early improvement in pregnancy-associated spontaneous coronary artery dissection, which complication remains a major concern?","options":["maternal and fetal death from prolonged low-flow state","recurrent seizure, intracranial haemorrhage and fetal hypoxia","DIC, fetal death and haemorrhagic shock","pulmonary oedema, arrhythmia and thromboembolism","maternal infarction, arrhythmia and cardiogenic shock"],"answerIndex":4,"answer":"maternal infarction, arrhythmia and cardiogenic shock","explanation":"The complication to anticipate is maternal infarction, arrhythmia and cardiogenic shock. Continued reassessment is required even after initial stabilisation of pregnancy-associated spontaneous coronary artery dissection.","learningPoint":"Pregnancy-associated spontaneous coronary artery dissection: coronary intramural haematoma or dissection in the pregnancy-associated period. Avoid giving fibrinolysis without considering coronary dissection.","id":"obstetrics-and-gynaecology-200","globalNumber":2670,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Medical Administration","categoryNumber":31,"type":"calculation","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A diagnostic study reports TP=88, FN=12, FP=27, and TN=173. What is the sensitivity?","options":["88.0%","93.5%","86.5%","87.0%","76.5%"],"answerIndex":0,"answer":"88.0%","explanation":"Sensitivity = TP/(TP+FN) = 88/100 = 88.0%.","learningPoint":"Sensitivity is the proportion of people with disease who test positive.","id":"medical-administration-031","globalNumber":2671,"questionSet":"Expansion 2026"},{"category":"Medical Administration","categoryNumber":32,"type":"calculation","difficulty":"5/5","stem":"A diagnostic study reports TP=143, FN=17, FP=41, and TN=199. What is the sensitivity?","options":["82.9%","89.